# Everything in docs/ is ignored unless it is named below.
#
# This directory holds both published documentation and internal material --
# `docs/specs/` and `docs/plans/`, which are never committed. A default-deny
# rule is the only arrangement where forgetting to act is safe: a new file
# added here is ignored until someone deliberately allowlists it, so the
# mistake mode is "a public doc is missing from the repo", which is visible
# and trivially fixed, rather than "an internal doc was published", which is
# not recoverable by deleting it.
#
# Copied from CoralMind/knowledge-library so the two repositories answer this
# question the same way. A contributor moving between them should not have to
# work out which one publishes its design notes.
#
# TO COMMIT A NEW FILE HERE: add a negation below, in the same commit that
# adds the file, and say in the commit message why it is publishable.
#
# Note that git cannot re-include a file inside an excluded directory, so a
# negation for something in a subdirectory needs the directory unignored too
# (`!sub/` before `!sub/file.md`). Every allowlisted file today sits directly
# in docs/, so that case does not arise yet.
*

!.gitignore
!sim-call-stack.md
